171 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (ECLA is a mid-sized nonprofit organization that serves as a hub for Ethiopian immigrants throughout California. It is governed by an eleven-member board, an executive director that oversees operations, and an advisory board that supports the board by advising on governance and policy. Our membership-based organization is accountable to its members through annual general assemblies and election boards that guide leadership selection.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
172 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Operating as a virtual nonprofit, ECLA partners with twenty-five local nonprofits and county offices to offer a range of services to its community. The membership spans across multiple zip codes and is primarily composed of older, bilingual individuals, many of whom have been in the U.S. for over 40 years, while others are recent arrivals needing assistance integrating into the greater society. Our services aim to address both short- and long-term needs through a variety of programs and services. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
173 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (With an annual revenue of $50,000 to $60,000, supplemented by small grants from banks and foundations, we organize 3-4 fundraising campaigns annually and sell merchandise at events. Our 3-4 contracted staff, alongside a dedicated group of 30-40 volunteers, work to deliver essential services. Additionally, we were awarded a $750,000 HUD grant 18 months ago, which we are working towards augmenting to purchase a center for the community.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
