/S /P
/ActualText (1. Mental Health Services: In collaboration with NAMI and LA County, we host workshops on topics such as suicide prevention and substance abuse. We have launched a monthly Young Adult Peer Support Group on Wednesdays, and a monthly Adult Support Group on Thursdays. Support Groups are facilitated by clinicians, associates, and social workers. We support local clinics by offering culturally appropriate mental health support through our network of Ethiopian clinicians. This coming year we would like to actively engage with community leaders to understand and address specific cultural or linguistic barriers to care. We plan to organize public events to promote mental health literacy and open conversations about mental well-being. 80 Assisted through Call Center)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
181 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (2. Medical Health: Most of our work revolves around finding medical resources, insurance access, and issues around Medicare benefits. We host health and annual insurance fairs at faith-based organizations and partner clinics, and match callers to health clinics. This coming year we plan to enhance access to healthcare for our underserved community members who lack resources by organizing community outreach programs and pro bono services. We will organize support groups on topics such as nutrition, exercise, and disease prevention. We will also address common parenting challenges, stress management, and coping strategies. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
182 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (40 Call Center/Insurance Fair)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
183 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (3. Immigration Services: We offer immigration-related workshops every eight weeks in partnership with BAJI and provide pro bono legal services and immigration clinics. Our call center serves as a key resource for immigration-related inquiries.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
184 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (We will continue to facilitate the integration of immigrants into the broader community by organizing events, workshops, and programs that encourage interactions, cultural exchange, and mutual understanding between immigrants and long-term residents to create an inclusive and welcoming environment. We will continue to establish strong partnerships and collaborations with legal clinics and community organizations to better support immigrants in the community and maximize its impact and improve the overall outcomes for immigrants. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
185 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (159 Referrals to Pro Bono Services)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
186 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (4. Senior Services: A weekly One Stop at the Inglewood Senior Center assists bilingual seniors with housing applications, insurance, nutrition, and transportation needs. Volunteers include retired professionals such as teachers, social workers, pharmacists, and nurses. One of our priorities is to build and maintain social connections by organizing regular social events and group outings. We will also work on hosting more workshops on topics like healthy aging, nutrition, and stress management. 200 Assisted at Senior Center/ through Call Center)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
187 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Ethiopian Community Los Angeles)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
188 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (5. Youth Services: We have moved our weekly Amharic language classes online and we are reaching more youth. We also offer STEM mentoring, tutoring, and sport clinics. We host multigenerational picnics to foster community involvement and this year we have launched a Young Adult Peer Space monthly support group, with the youth driving the agenda. We will move forward with career exploration workshops and internships to equip youth with the skills, knowledge, and networks necessary for successful career paths. 130 Participants)
/E (5. Youth Services: We have moved our weekly Amharic language classes online and we are reaching more youth. We also offer STEM mentoring, tutoring, and sport clinics. We host multigenerational picnics to foster community involvement and this year we have launched a Young Adult Peer Space monthly support group, with the youth driving the agenda. We will move forward with career exploration workshops and internships to equip youth with the skills, knowledge, and networks necessary for successful career paths. 130 Participants)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
189 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (6. Social/Cultural Services: ECLA hosts annual cultural events, including fundraising dinners, festivals, book signings, and picnics. We will continue to celebrate Ethiopian traditions, customs, music, dance, art, and cuisine to foster a sense of pride among community members and help preserve Ethiopian heritage for future generations. This year we look forward to partnering with other cultural and community organizations to promote cross- cultural understanding and inclusivity within the wider community, to foster mutual respect and appreciation for diversity. 12,355 Engagement with ECLA)
/E (6. Social/Cultural Services: ECLA hosts annual cultural events, including fundraising dinners, festivals, book signings, and picnics. We will continue to celebrate Ethiopian traditions, customs, music, dance, art, and cuisine to foster a sense of pride among community members and help preserve Ethiopian heritage for future generations. This year we look forward to partnering with other cultural and community organizations to promote cross- cultural understanding and inclusivity within the wider community, to foster mutual respect and appreciation for diversity. 12,355 Engagement with ECLA)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
